## THE QUESTION (read WHOLE first)
KS-2283 on the Secuura Linear board (read its description whole). F1 in short, with the lines read at develop 70a0d984ac70: line 106-109 area of the test file: the cell `RED ks1936 org-admin with a malformed JSON body is refused with 403 (not 400) and no query` has the comment at line 108 ("Precondition: the parser really rejects this body (a platform role gets 400)...") and the assertion at line 109, `expect((await patchRaw('system-admin', broken)).status).toBe(400);`. `patchRaw` (line 81) returns `{status, text}`. The precondition checks the status only; the handler answers 400 with the code `BAD_REQUEST` for `{}`, while the real parser answers 400 with an HTML `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input` (measured by gate 383). The ticket's fix shape (the builder's choice): assert the platform admin's reply is not the handler's own refusal (for example `expect(text).not.toContain('BAD_REQUEST')`) or that it carries the parser's error; then run the G12 variant and confirm the cell fails.
**F2 is NOT built:** PR 2260 is merged and its body is not edited; KS-2278 holds the correction (originate's copy is reachable on the `/originate/` path). The only F2 action is a sentence in your ONE facts comment saying so.

